# Deterministic line endings for checksum-sensitive data and tooling.
#
# Pass 2A finding: on Windows checkouts core.autocrlf converted these LF-committed
# files to CRLF in the working tree. Content hashes (e.g. the USDA selection and
# catalogue contracts) are computed over parsed JSON so they were never at risk,
# but byte-level checkout drift made verification noisy and non-reproducible.
# Pinning these globs to LF makes the working-tree bytes equal the committed bytes
# on every platform without rewriting any stored blob or changing any valid hash.

*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
